WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:09.130
Before visitors arrive, a basket of clean laundry leaves the couch. Most of what is moved goes to one room, and the door is closed.

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:13.920
A doctoral thesis from the School of Continuous Improvement asks what is moved,

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:15.180
and where it goes.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:21.190
For twenty-six weeks, sixty-one households wrote down everything they carried before a visit.

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:24.040
I drew each home to scale, and measured every route.

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:29.080
Twenty-five thousand and thirty-three moves, in nine hundred and fifty-two tidies.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:32.250
Seventy-nine per cent put an object out of sight, not away.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:34.540
Sixty-one per cent went to a single room.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:36.740
Then I asked the visitors.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.600
Their ratings didn't follow the time spent tidying.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:43.610
Fifty-eight of a hundred and twenty-four recalled a closed door,

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:45.410
and three wondered what was behind it.

00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:51.140
In a trial, households were granted that room in advance, with a card on its door.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:54.700
Their median tidy fell from forty-six minutes to twenty-eight,

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.720
and visitors rated the homes the same.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:03.090
But by week twelve, the room held a median of a hundred and eighteen objects, up from forty-four.

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:08.100
In seventeen of twenty-four homes, it could not be used for its own purpose on any day.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.644
The School adopted the arrangement unchanged, as the Closed Door Allowance,

00:01:13.844 --> 00:01:15.984
now extended to every unit of the University.

00:01:16.384 --> 00:01:19.044
The reviewing party does not open a registered door.

00:01:19.244 --> 00:01:22.654
No finding is drawn from a room the reviewing party did not enter.

00:01:24.054 --> 00:01:30.624
The distance between a home as it is shown and a home as it is lived in is, on that record, a few metres and a door.
